{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-003", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh to revive 3 jute mills with $50 mn private investment", "content": "Bangladesh has signed leases with PRAN-RFL Group and a second private group to restart three BJMC jute mills in Sirajganj and Khulna. \nThe projects carry Tk 6.19 billion in planned investment and at least 11,629 jobs, signalling potential fresh capacity for jute supply chains. \nThe wider programme targets reopening 20 of 25 closed BJMC mills; 14 leases are complete and nine mills have resumed. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-to-revive-3-jute-mills-with-50-mn-private-investment-312570-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-004", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Ralph Lauren crushes Q1 2026: Stock jumps 7% on strong sales", "content": "Ralph Lauren's first-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue reached $1.96 billion, with adjusted earnings of $4.59 a share and constant-currency revenue up 13 per cent.\nAsia led growth at 25 per cent, with China up more than 40 per cent; North America rose 13 per cent and Europe gained 5 per cent.\nFull-year revenue outlook is now 5–6 per cent, with tariffs and soft Europe sentiment flagged.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ralph-lauren-crushes-q1-2026-stock-jumps-7-on-strong-sales-312567-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-005", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh PMI rises sharply as manufacturing hits series high in July", "content": "Bangladesh's composite PMI rose 4.9 points to 57.8 in July, moving further above the 50-point expansion mark. \nManufacturing jumped 16.6 points to 65.4, with gains across orders, exports, output, employment, imports and deliveries. \nFor garment and textile supply chains, stronger exports and improved expectations signal firmer near-term factory activity. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-pmi-rises-sharply-as-manufacturing-hits-series-high-in-july-312564-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-006", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "VSF's stable prices set the stage for a mid-August price breakout", "content": "VSF markets in India, China and Pakistan closed August 3–10 in near-perfect stability, with TexPro benchmarks flat in India and China.\nIndia's 1.4D and 1.5D×38mm VSF held at ₹196/kg and ₹193/kg, while China's 1.5D×38mm stayed at CNY 14.25/kg.\nPakistan's 1.5D grade eased from PKR 639/kg to PKR 638/kg, a 0.16 per cent move linked to rupee rounding rather than fundamental pressure.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vsf-s-stable-prices-set-the-stage-for-a-mid-august-price-breakout-312565-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-007", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam targets 1500 containers/year in rail freight service to China", "content": "The rail freight route linking China’s Hebei province with Vietnam has delivered encouraging results after more than a year of operation, with improved supply chain efficiency, reduced logistics costs and transit times, and more opportunities for businesses, according to Vietnam Railway Transport. \nThe firm is working with partners to further develop the service, targeting around 1,500 containers annually. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-targets-1500-containers-year-in-rail-freight-service-to-china-312563-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-12-008", "date": "2026-08-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s cotton pressing revised upward to 339 lakh bales: CAI", "content": "Cotton Association of India has raised current-season cotton pressing to 339 lakh bales, 11 per cent above its initial estimate of 305 lakh bales.\nThe latest estimate is 8.5 per cent higher than 2024–25, with increases in Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Karnataka and Tamil Nadu.\nImports are projected at 62 lakh bales and closing stocks at 93.59 lakh bales by September 30, 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-cotton-pressing-revised-upward-to-339-lakh-bales-cai-312560-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
